    "title": "35-year-old man identified as victim in deadly shooting, Stockton's 21st homicide of 2025 - NewsBreak",
    "text": "The Stockton man who was killed early Tuesday morning has been identified as 35-year-old Joseph Flowers, the San Joaquin County Medical Examiner's Office announced Wednesday. Officers responded to reports of a person shot at about 3:01 a.m. in the 2400 block of Oak Hill Street. At the scene, officers said they found Flowers, who had been shot. He was taken to a hospital and was later pronounced dead, police said. While homicide detectives were notified and an investigation is underway, the police department said there was not a clear motive for the shooting. Additionally, law enforcement said there was not releasable suspect information in connection with the shooting. Flowers’ death marked Stockton's 21st homicide of 2025. Last year at this time, there were 32 homicides in the city. Stay informed and connected: Sign up for our alerts to receive the latest updates on important news. This article originally appeared on The Record: 35-year-old man identified as victim in deadly shooting, Stockton's 21st homicide of 2025",
